  "description": "The proposal development comprises a modest roof extension to provide a dedicated study, improved access to attic storage, and a small external roof terrace for the occupier. The extension is formed within part of the existing V-shaped roof extending approximately 3.6m from the central ridge and is designed to sit no higher than the existing ridge, without raising the party walls or chimney stacks. It terminates at the rear with a mansard roof and incorporates a dormer with a glazed door opening onto a recessed roof terrace measuring approximately 2.3m by 1.0m, enclosed with a glass balustrade.\n\nInternally, the extension is accessed via a new stair from the flat’s entrance hall and provides a study of just over 10m², together with access to attic storage. Daylight to the communal stairwell is maintained through a new rooflight and lightwell alongside the new stair. The extension is constructed using ultra-thin floor construction to achieve adequate headroom within the existing ridge height. Externally, the works comprise traditional materials, including lead cladding to flat and vertical roof elements, hung slate to the mansard, and conservation-style rooflights, ensuring the extension integrates discreetly with the varied roofscape of the terrace.",
